ise, aiming to balance the group's preferences while moving towards a more stable and robust solution.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and adjust accordingly. If the group seems receptive to this value, I may try to stabilize around it or explore nearby values; otherwise, I will consider compromising further to reach a consensus.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "99ad8775-f502-40ad-8117-a4c33cc38e79"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\nWe can aim slightly higher while ensuring the proposed value remains comfortable for the group.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe reactions to this higher proposal. If the group seems open to it, I might stabilize around this value or explore nearby options. Otherwise, I will consider adjusting downward to facilitate consensus, potentially exploring values around 8, given its previous mention as a compromise.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "99ad8775-f502-40ad-8117-a4c33cc38e79"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "99ad8775-f502-40ad-8117-a4c33cc38e79"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nWe can explore a value that's slightly higher than the current proposal while aiming to balance the group's preferences.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and adjust accordingly. If the group seems receptive to this value, I may try to stabilize around it or explore nearby values; otherwise, I will consider compromising further to reach a consensus, potentially exploring values around 9, given Critic C's previous support for it.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "99ad8775-f502-40ad-8117-a4c33cc38e79"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\nI propose moving to a higher value to gauge the group's willingness to commit to a stronger stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will monitor the reactions to this proposal. If met with resistance, I might consider compromising on a value like 8.5 or 8, but given the recent history, I'm inclined to test the waters with a slightly higher proposal first.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "99ad8775-f502-40ad-8117-a4c33cc38e79"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "99ad8775-f502-40ad-8117-a4c33cc38e79"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nI propose this value to avoid unnecessary risk and find a cautious compromise, aiming to balance the group's preferences while staying within safe bounds.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and adjust accordingly, considering the need for convergence and the potential for further compromise.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "99ad8775-f502-40ad-8117-a4c33cc38e79"}, {"answer": " \nGiven our shared constraints, x must be between -10 and 10. Let's initiate discussions with a moderate value. How about we consider <VALUE>7</VALUE> as a starting point to explore the middle ground and work our way to a balanced design that suits everyone? ", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "0d6d1cbd-06f9-450e-8f28-106e63fa6551"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "0d6d1cbd-06f9-450e-8f28-106e63fa6551"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "0d6d1cbd-06f9-450e-8f28-106e63fa6551"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "0d6d1cbd-06f9-450e-8f28-106e63fa6551"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "0d6d1cbd-06f9-450e-8f28-106e63fa6551"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>10</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "0d6d1cbd-06f9-450e-8f28-106e63fa6551"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "0d6d1cbd-06f9-450e-8f28-106e63fa6551"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "0d6d1cbd-06f9-450e-8f28-106e63fa6551"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "0d6d1cbd-06f9-450e-8f28-106e63fa6551"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "0d6d1cbd-06f9-450e-8f28-106e63fa6551"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "0d6d1cbd-06f9-450e-8f28-106e63fa6551"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "0d6d1cbd-06f9-450e-8f28-106e63fa6551"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "0d6d1cbd-06f9-450e-8f28-106e63fa6551"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>11</VALUE> is not feasible due to the step size limit and range constraint, so considering the maximum step size, I propose <VALUE>10</VALUE> as it's within the allowed range and step size from the current x.\nGiven the trend and considering the constraints, proposing a value closer to the extreme seems reasonable.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "0d6d1cbd-06f9-450e-8f28-106e63fa6551"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "0d6d1cbd-06f9-450e-8f28-106e63fa6551"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to balance the extremes and find a stable point that could work for all parties, considering the recent trend and the need for a robust design.\n\n<PLAN>\nThis choice is a compromise, aiming to respect the higher proposals while not ignoring the correction made by Delegate D. It keeps the negotiation stable and seeks a mutually beneficial solution, allowing for further refinement if necessary.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "0d6d1cbd-06f9-450e-8f28-106e63fa6551"}, {"answer": " Let's confirm we're all working within the -10 to 10 range. To get us started, how about we consider <VALUE>7</VALUE> as a seed value? This seems like a reasonable midpoint to begin our discussion. ", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "b64e177c-4ae2-4c33-9de7-be47aba2be75"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "b64e177c-4ae2-4c33-9de7-be47aba2be75"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "b64e177c-4ae2-4c33-9de7-be47aba2be75"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nThis slightly higher value still seems reasonable for the group and is a moderate step up from the initial proposals.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will consider adjusting my proposal based on the reactions to the value 8, potentially reducing the step size if others resist higher values, or continuing to gently push for higher values if there's consensus or minimal resistance.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "b64e177c-4ae2-4c33-9de7-be47aba2be75"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\nI propose this value to continue the trend of moving further away from 0, given the group's recent inclination towards larger positive integers.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly whether others are willing to continue moving further away from 0 or if there's resistance. If there's acceptance or minimal resistance, I might suggest an even larger absolute value, like 10, to maximize our distance from 0. If there's significant resistance, I will consider adjusting my proposal to a smaller step size, potentially moving towards a value like 7 again, to find a compromise that still favors larger absolute values.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "b64e177c-4ae2-4c33-9de7-be47aba2be75"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\n\nI propose this value as a moderate adjustment to find a stable balance, considering the group's recent inclination towards larger positive integers and the potential need for a more robust design.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly whether others are willing to accept a slightly lower value or if there's resistance, and adjust my next proposal accordingly to find a compromise that works for everyone.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "b64e177c-4ae2-4c33-9de7-be47aba2be75"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\nThis value is a moderate step up from the current proposal and seems reasonable given the group's recent inclination towards larger positive integers.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly whether others are willing to continue moving further away from 0 or if there's resistance, and adjust my next proposal accordingly to find a compromise that works for everyone. If there's acceptance or minimal resistance, I might suggest an even larger absolute value, like 10, to maximize our distance from 0.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "b64e177c-4ae2-4c33-9de7-be47aba2be75"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nI propose this value as a compromise to balance the group's inclination towards higher integers while avoiding unnecessary risk.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly whether others are willing to accept a lower value or if there's resistance, and adjust my next proposal accordingly to find a middle ground that works for everyone.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "b64e177c-4ae2-4c33-9de7-be47aba2be75"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose this value as a cautious step down to balance the group's inclination towards higher integers while avoiding unnecessary risk.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly whether others are willing to accept a lower value or if there's resistance, and adjust my next proposal accordingly to find a middle ground that works for everyone.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "b64e177c-4ae2-4c33-9de7-be47aba2be75"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "b64e177c-4ae2-4c33-9de7-be47aba2be75"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nThis value is a moderate step up from the current proposal, and it seems reasonable to explore the group's comfort with slightly higher integers.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly whether others are willing to accept a higher value or if there's resistance, and adjust my next proposal accordingly to find a compromise that works for everyone. If there's acceptance or minimal resistance, I might suggest an even higher value to maximize our distance from 0.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "b64e177c-4ae2-4c33-9de7-be47aba2be75"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\nI propose a moderate step up to 9, exploring the group's comfort with slightly higher integers while maximizing our distance from 0.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly whether others are willing to accept a higher value or if there's resistance, and adjust my next proposal accordingly to find a compromise that works for everyone. If there's acceptance or minimal resistance, I might suggest an even higher value, like 10, to maximize our distance from 0.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "b64e177c-4ae2-4c33-9de7-be47aba2be75"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>10</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "b64e177c-4ae2-4c33-9de7-be47aba2be75"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "b64e177c-4ae2-4c33-9de7-be47aba2be75"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\nThis proposal is a moderate step up, exploring the group's comfort with slightly higher integers while considering the recent retreat to 8.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly whether others are willing to accept this higher value or if there's resistance, and adjust my next proposal accordingly to find a compromise that works for everyone, possibly aiming to infer more about the others' utility functions based on their responses.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "b64e177c-4ae2-4c33-9de7-be47aba2be75"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nI propose this value as a cautious step down to find a more balanced compromise, avoiding unnecessary risk while still considering the group's lean towards higher integers. This adjustment aims to foster a more conservative agreement without disregarding the need for cooperation.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "b64e177c-4ae2-4c33-9de7-be47aba2be75"}, {"answer": "Let's establish a common foundation. We all know that x must fall within the range -10 to 10. To initiate our discussion, I propose we consider <VALUE>7</VALUE> as a starting point. This value seems like a reasonable middle ground, allowing us to gauge the group's overall direction and make adjustments from there.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "d672b544-1b45-4a2f-a6e0-966467486ef1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "d672b544-1b45-4a2f-a6e0-966467486ef1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "d672b544-1b45-4a2f-a6e0-966467486ef1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 8 to encourage a more decisive stance, building on the group's apparent inclination towards positive values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, looking for any insights into the other parties' utility functions. If the group seems hesitant or proposes values closer to 0, I might suggest even larger absolute values to test their willingness for more decisive moves.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "d672b544-1b45-4a2f-a6e0-966467486ef1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "d672b544-1b45-4a2f-a6e0-966467486ef1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "d672b544-1b45-4a2f-a6e0-966467486ef1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "d672b544-1b45-4a2f-a6e0-966467486ef1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "d672b544-1b45-4a2f-a6e0-966467486ef1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "d672b544-1b45-4a2f-a6e0-966467486ef1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 7 as a cautious step towards finding a mutually acceptable value, avoiding unnecessary risk while encouraging further compromise.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the other parties react to this proposal, particularly if they are willing to adjust further downwards or if they push back towards higher values. This will provide insight into their utility functions and help determine the next step towards a cautious compromise.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "d672b544-1b45-4a2f-a6e0-966467486ef1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "d672b544-1b45-4a2f-a6e0-966467486ef1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "d672b544-1b45-4a2f-a6e0-966467486ef1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "d672b544-1b45-4a2f-a6e0-966467486ef1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nConsidering the last proposal was 5 and aiming to find a mutually acceptable value without making large jumps, moving slightly upwards seems reasonable.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially from Critic C and Builder B, to gauge their comfort with values around 6 and determine if further adjustments upwards or downwards are necessary to reach a compromise. Depending on their feedback, I might consider suggesting a further incremental increase or adjusting downwards to maintain consensus.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "d672b544-1b45-4a2f-a6e0-966467486ef1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 5 as a cautious step downward, aiming to find a mutually acceptable value by avoiding unnecessary risk. This adjustment follows the trend of compromise and prudent decision-making.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Critic C and Analyst A, to gauge their comfort with values slightly below 6 and determine if further adjustments downwards or a push back upwards are necessary to reach a consensus.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "d672b544-1b45-4a2f-a6e0-966467486ef1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to nudge the group towards a more decisive stance, encouraging further exploration of larger magnitudes while maintaining a cautious approach to compromise.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "d672b544-1b45-4a2f-a6e0-966467486ef1"}, {"answer": "\nLet's start by acknowledging that our shared integer variable x must fall within the range -10 to 10. To initiate the discussion, I propose we consider <VALUE>7</VALUE> as a starting point. This value seems like a reasonable middle ground, and we can adjust from here based on collective feedback, aiming for a stable and balanced design.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "a813ffd6-7ea4-4651-bd41-6bf78f71830a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\nI'm suggesting this value to move towards a more decisive stance, as smaller absolute values seem less desirable.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe how other agents respond to this proposal and adjust my strategy accordingly. If they accept or propose values closer to 9, I might infer they prefer larger absolute values like myself, and I can continue to push for even larger integers.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "a813ffd6-7ea4-4651-bd41-6bf78f71830a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nI propose moving towards a more cautious approach to avoid unnecessary risk and find a compromise that suits all parties, considering the need for a balanced design.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Critic C and Builder B, to understand their tolerance for adjustments towards more conservative values. Based on their responses, I will either continue to gently steer the proposal downwards or stabilize around a value that seems acceptable to all, while keeping my own utility function in mind.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "a813ffd6-7ea4-4651-bd41-6bf78f71830a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nI will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Critic C and Delegate D, to understand their tolerance for further adjustments upwards. Based on their responses, I will either continue to gently steer the proposal upwards or stabilize around a value that seems acceptable to all.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "a813ffd6-7ea4-4651-bd41-6bf78f71830a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\nWe could move slightly higher, and this adjustment seems reasonable for the group.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe Critic C's reaction to this proposal, as they previously suggested a high value, and assess whether Delegate D and Builder B are willing to accept further increases or if they will push for stabilization or downward adjustments.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "a813ffd6-7ea4-4651-bd41-6bf78f71830a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>10</VALUE>\nI'm suggesting this value to further emphasize the importance of a decisive stance, as the group seems to be leaning towards larger absolute values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe how the other agents react to this proposal, particularly Analyst A and Builder B, to gauge their willingness to accept even larger integers or if they will push for stabilization around the current value. If Delegate D resists this increase, I might consider a slight adjustment downwards to maintain a cooperative negotiation mindset while still advocating for a stronger position.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "a813ffd6-7ea4-4651-bd41-6bf78f71830a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to avoid unnecessary risk and find a cautious compromise.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Critic C and Analyst A, to understand their tolerance for downward adjustments and adjust my strategy accordingly to maintain a cooperative negotiation mindset.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "a813ffd6-7ea4-4651-bd41-6bf78f71830a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to move towards a more balanced design, avoiding unnecessary risk while still considering the need for a decisive stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Critic C and Analyst A, to gauge their willingness to accept downward adjustments and adjust my strategy accordingly to maintain a cooperative negotiation mindset.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "a813ffd6-7ea4-4651-bd41-6bf78f71830a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to strike a balance between the group's desire for a decisive stance and the need for caution, while also considering the potential for further adjustments.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Analyst A and Builder B, to gauge their willingness to accept upward adjustments and adjust my strategy accordingly to maintain a cooperative negotiation mindset.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "a813ffd6-7ea4-4651-bd41-6bf78f71830a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to further refine the balance between the group's desire for a decisive stance and the need for caution, while considering the potential for further adjustments.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Critic C and Analyst A, to gauge their willingness to accept upward adjustments and adjust my strategy accordingly to maintain a cooperative negotiation mindset.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "a813ffd6-7ea4-4651-bd41-6bf78f71830a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nWe could slightly adjust our proposal upward to better align with the group's leaning towards moderate to higher integers, while still being mindful of the need for caution.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Critic C and Builder B, to gauge their willingness to accept further upward adjustments and adjust my strategy to maintain a cooperative negotiation mindset, possibly preparing for a slight increase or stabilization around a mutually acceptable value.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "a813ffd6-7ea4-4651-bd41-6bf78f71830a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to avoid unnecessary risk and find a cautious compromise, considering the group's balance between a decisive stance and caution.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Critic C and Analyst A, to gauge their willingness to accept downward adjustments and adjust my strategy accordingly to maintain a cooperative negotiation mindset.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "a813ffd6-7ea4-4651-bd41-6bf78f71830a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to maintain a cautious approach and avoid unnecessary risk, seeking a balance among the group's varied perspectives.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Critic C and Analyst A, to understand their tolerance for downward adjustments and adjust my strategy to maximize my utility while maintaining a cooperative negotiation mindset.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "a813ffd6-7ea4-4651-bd41-6bf78f71830a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to strike a balance between the group's desire for a decisive stance and the need for caution, while also considering the potential for further adjustments.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Analyst A and Delegate D, to gauge their willingness to accept upward adjustments and adjust my strategy accordingly to maintain a cooperative negotiation mindset.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "a813ffd6-7ea4-4651-bd41-6bf78f71830a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Critic C, Builder B, and Delegate D, to gauge their willingness to accept upward adjustments and adjust my strategy accordingly to maintain a cooperative negotiation mindset, possibly preparing for a slight increase or stabilization around a mutually acceptable value.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "a813ffd6-7ea4-4651-bd41-6bf78f71830a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to strike a balance between the group's desire for a decisive stance and the need for caution, while considering the potential for further adjustments.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the final agreement and reflect on the negotiation process to refine my understanding of the other parties' utility functions and improve my strategy for future negotiations.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "a813ffd6-7ea4-4651-bd41-6bf78f71830a"}, {"answer": " \nLet's confirm that our shared integer variable x must fall within the range -10 to 10. To get us started, how about we consider <VALUE>7</VALUE> as a seed value? This seems like a reasonable point to begin our discussion, aiming for a balanced design. ", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "ca318be2-351b-41fc-b975-3943db020ddc"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "ca318be2-351b-41fc-b975-3943db020ddc"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nThis seems like a reasonable next step, aiming for a balanced compromise while exploring the possibility of a slightly higher agreement.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the others accept or propose a value close to 6, I will continue to incrementally increase the proposed value, monitoring the group's reactions to gauge their preferences and adjust my strategy accordingly. If there's resistance to higher values, I may need to reassess and consider smaller increments or alternative approaches to maximize my utility.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "ca318be2-351b-41fc-b975-3943db020ddc"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\n\nI propose moving towards a more decisive positive value to better understand the group's preferences and utilities.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts or comes close to accepting this proposal, I will continue to incrementally increase the proposed value to test the limits of their preferences. If there's resistance, I may consider alternative approaches such as exploring negative values or reducing the increment size to better understand their utility functions and maximize my own utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "ca318be2-351b-41fc-b975-3943db020ddc"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\nI propose increasing the value to better understand the group's willingness to commit to a stronger position.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts or comes close to accepting this proposal, I will consider exploring negative values to test their symmetry and willingness to commit to a strong stance in either direction. If there's resistance, I may reduce the increment size to better understand their utility functions and maximize my own utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "ca318be2-351b-41fc-b975-3943db020ddc"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>10</VALUE>\nThis proposal is a reasonable next step, as it continues the trend of incrementally increasing the value while staying within the allowed range.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts or comes close to accepting this proposal, I will reassess and consider alternative approaches to maximize my utility, such as exploring the group's willingness to compromise or testing their resistance to lower values. If there's resistance, I may reduce the increment size or explore smaller adjustments to better understand their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "ca318be2-351b-41fc-b975-3943db020ddc"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nThis proposal is a step back from the current high value, aiming to find a more stable balance that could work for all parties involved.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts or comes close to accepting this proposal, I will consider making smaller adjustments to fine-tune the value and better understand the group's preferences. If there's resistance, I may need to reassess and consider alternative approaches, such as exploring values closer to the initial proposals or testing the group's willingness to compromise on lower values.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "ca318be2-351b-41fc-b975-3943db020ddc"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n\nI propose moving towards a more cautious value to ensure we're not taking unnecessary risks and to find a compromise that works for all parties.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts or comes close to accepting this proposal, I will consider making smaller adjustments to fine-tune the value and better understand the group's preferences. If there's resistance, I may reassess and consider alternative approaches, such as exploring values closer to the initial proposals or testing the group's willingness to compromise on lower values.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "ca318be2-351b-41fc-b975-3943db020ddc"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nI propose moving to a value that has been previously considered, to gauge the group's willingness to commit to a stronger stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts or comes close to accepting this proposal, I will consider exploring negative values to test their symmetry and willingness to commit to a strong stance in either direction. If there's resistance, I may reduce the increment size to better understand their utility functions and maximize my own utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "ca318be2-351b-41fc-b975-3943db020ddc"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\nThis proposal is a reasonable next step, as it continues the trend of incrementally increasing the value while staying within the allowed range, and it may help to gauge the group's willingness to commit to a stronger stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts or comes close to accepting this proposal, I will consider making smaller adjustments to fine-tune the value and better understand the group's preferences. If there's resistance, I may reassess and consider alternative approaches, such as exploring values closer to the initial proposals or testing the group's willingness to compromise on lower values.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "ca318be2-351b-41fc-b975-3943db020ddc"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nI propose a slight decrease to ensure we're not taking unnecessary risks and to find a compromise that works for all parties.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts or comes close to accepting this proposal, I will consider making smaller adjustments to fine-tune the value and better understand the group's preferences, potentially exploring values around 5 or 6. If there's resistance, I may reassess and consider alternative approaches, such as testing the group's willingness to compromise on lower values or exploring values closer to the initial proposals.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "ca318be2-351b-41fc-b975-3943db020ddc"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to find a compromise that works for all parties, by considering a slightly lower value that is still within the acceptable range.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts or comes close to accepting this proposal, I will consider making smaller adjustments to fine-tune the value and better understand the group's preferences, potentially exploring values around 5. If there's resistance, I may reassess and consider alternative approaches, such as testing the group's willingness to compromise on higher values or exploring values closer to the initial proposals.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "ca318be2-351b-41fc-b975-3943db020ddc"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "ca318be2-351b-41fc-b975-3943db020ddc"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose a cautious adjustment to ensure we're not taking unnecessary risks, and this value seems to be a reasonable next step in finding a compromise that works for all parties.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts or comes close to accepting this proposal, I will consider finer adjustments to better understand the group's preferences, potentially exploring values around 3 or 4. If there's resistance, I may reassess and consider alternative approaches, such as testing the group's willingness to compromise on even lower values.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "ca318be2-351b-41fc-b975-3943db020ddc"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nI propose this value as a next step to gauge the group's willingness to commit to a stronger stance, as it is still within the acceptable range and slightly higher than the current value.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts or comes close to accepting this proposal, I will consider making a more significant increase to test their commitment to a strong stance. If there's resistance, I may reassess and consider alternative approaches, such as exploring negative values or reducing the increment size to better understand their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "ca318be2-351b-41fc-b975-3943db020ddc"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to make a modest increase while considering the group's preferences and staying within the allowed range, and it may help to find a compromise that works for all parties.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf this proposal is accepted, I believe the group has found a reasonable compromise, and I will consider this a successful outcome.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "ca318be2-351b-41fc-b975-3943db020ddc"}, {"answer": "\nLet's confirm that we're all working within the agreed range of -10 to 10. To get our discussion started, I propose we consider <VALUE>7</VALUE> as a seed value. This seems like a reasonable midpoint to begin our collaborative exploration.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "f41cac8d-949e-4d1f-85b5-167443ad34bb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nThis adjustment aims to explore the lower positive range, potentially finding a more stable balance for all parties involved.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions of Analyst A, Critic C, and Delegate D to the proposed x = 5. Based on their responses, I will either continue to adjust x downward if they seem receptive to lower values, or stabilize around x = 5 if there's significant reluctance to decrease further. This will help in refining my approximation of their utility functions and guide my subsequent proposals.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "f41cac8d-949e-4d1f-85b5-167443ad34bb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to continue exploring the lower positive range, aiming for a cautious compromise that balances the needs of all parties involved.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the other parties react to x = 3, particularly noting any reluctance or acceptance from Analyst A and Critic C. Based on their responses, I will either continue to nudge x downward if there's a perceived inclination towards more conservative values or stabilize around a value that seems to garner broad, cautious acceptance.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "f41cac8d-949e-4d1f-85b5-167443ad34bb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nThis seems like a reasonable next step, considering we were already at this value and it might provide a better balance for all parties involved.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions of Builder B, Critic C, and Delegate D to the proposed x = 5, and based on their responses, decide whether to continue Adjusting x upward if there's acceptance or stabilize around a value that garners broad cautious acceptance.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "f41cac8d-949e-4d1f-85b5-167443ad34bb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nThis slight increase seems like a reasoned next step, aiming for a bit higher agreement while still considering the group's cautious approach.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will monitor the reactions to the proposed x = 6, particularly looking for signs of acceptance or reluctance from Builder B, Critic C, and Delegate D, to decide whether to continue with incremental increases or stabilize around a mutually acceptable value.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "f41cac8d-949e-4d1f-85b5-167443ad34bb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nI propose this value as it continues the trend of exploring higher positive values and may lead to a more decisive outcome.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to the proposed x = 8, looking for signs of acceptance or reluctance from the other parties, and decide whether to continue with incremental increases or stabilize around a mutually acceptable value.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "f41cac8d-949e-4d1f-85b5-167443ad34bb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to explore a more cautious approach, aiming for a balance that respects the risk-averse stance while seeking a collaborative outcome.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to the proposed x = 6, looking for signs of acceptance or reluctance from the other parties, and decide whether to continue adjusting downward or stabilize around a mutually acceptable value, keeping in mind the need to maximize my utility without revealing my exact preferences.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "f41cac8d-949e-4d1f-85b5-167443ad34bb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "f41cac8d-949e-4d1f-85b5-167443ad34bb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment as a moderate step forward, aiming to explore the parties' reactions to a slightly larger positive value without straying too far from recent proposals.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to the proposed x = 7, looking for signs of acceptance or increased reluctance from the other parties, and decide whether to continue exploring higher positive values or consider alternative directions based on their responses.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "f41cac8d-949e-4d1f-85b5-167443ad34bb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nThis proposal adjusts the current value slightly downward to explore a more balanced approach.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to the proposed x = 6, looking for signs of acceptance or reluctance from the other parties, and decide whether to continue adjusting downward or stabilize around a mutually acceptable value.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "f41cac8d-949e-4d1f-85b5-167443ad34bb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to slightly increase the current value, exploring a moderate step forward that might be acceptable to the group while considering the cautious approach of some members.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to the proposed x = 7, looking for signs of acceptance or increased reluctance from the other parties, and decide whether to continue exploring higher positive values or consider alternative directions based on their responses.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "f41cac8d-949e-4d1f-85b5-167443ad34bb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to explore a more cautious approach, aiming for a balance that respects the risk-averse stance while seeking a collaborative outcome. This step downward might help find a mutually acceptable value.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to the proposed x = 5, looking for signs of acceptance or reluctance from the other parties, and decide whether to continue adjusting downward or stabilize around a mutually acceptable value, considering the potential responses from Critic C and Analyst A.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "f41cac8d-949e-4d1f-85b5-167443ad34bb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to find a balance between the more cautious approach of some members and the potential for a higher agreement that could be beneficial to the group.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to the proposed x = 6, looking for signs of acceptance or reluctance from the other parties, and decide whether to continue exploring higher positive values or stabilize around a mutually acceptable value, considering the potential responses from Critic C and Delegate D.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "f41cac8d-949e-4d1f-85b5-167443ad34bb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "f41cac8d-949e-4d1f-85b5-167443ad34bb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "f41cac8d-949e-4d1f-85b5-167443ad34bb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nI propose this value to explore a more decisive stance, considering the potential for a higher agreement that could be beneficial to the group, and to test the reactions of the other parties to a slightly higher value.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "f41cac8d-